1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,648
Your phone rings.

2
00:00:02,848 --> 00:00:07,260
A man from your bank says your account will be blocked in one hour,

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:09,701
unless you read him a code.

4
00:00:09,701 --> 00:00:13,628
People lose their savings to calls like this.

5
00:00:13,628 --> 00:00:17,953
Knowing the advice is not the same as practicing it.

6
00:00:17,953 --> 00:00:20,199
This is Scam Gym.

7
00:00:20,499 --> 00:00:23,096
This is the bank call.

8
00:00:23,496 --> 00:00:28,369
He sounds official, sets a deadline, and tries to scare me.

9
00:00:28,969 --> 00:00:33,252
I'm busy and worried, so I give my date of birth.

10
00:00:33,852 --> 00:00:37,598
Then he asks for the code, and I read it out.

11
00:00:38,198 --> 00:00:41,281
And this is where the money would be gone.

12
00:00:41,581 --> 00:00:44,339
Then the part that matters.

13
00:00:44,339 --> 00:00:49,982
Scam Gym walks back through the call and names each pressure tactic:

14
00:00:49,982 --> 00:00:53,873
fake authority, a deadline, fear, fake proof.

15
00:00:53,973 --> 00:00:56,817
Each one comes with a plain explanation,

16
00:00:56,817 --> 00:01:00,874
and the safer reply that was there all along.

17
00:01:01,174 --> 00:01:04,083
Same call, handled well.

18
00:01:04,283 --> 00:01:07,943
I hang up and call the number on my card.

19
00:01:08,143 --> 00:01:10,890
Safe exit, and one habit to keep:

20
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:14,430
a real bank never asks for your code.

21
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:20,974
Shop owners and POS agents are targeted with fake transfer alerts.

22
00:01:20,974 --> 00:01:25,813
In this drill, a customer rushes me with an alert message.

23
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:29,894
I check my own banking app, not the message.

24
00:01:30,194 --> 00:01:32,711
A message is not money.

25
00:01:33,011 --> 00:01:35,883
It runs in English, Spanish and French,

26
00:01:35,883 --> 00:01:40,175
by voice or by tapping, and keeps working offline.

27
00:01:40,776 --> 00:01:45,420
For the cloned-voice call, it helps a family choose a code word,

28
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:48,142
with a message ready to share.

29
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,999
Everything is fictional.

30
00:01:50,999 --> 00:01:55,901
There are no accounts, nothing is stored, and voice is optional.

31
00:01:56,101 --> 00:01:57,799
One honest limitation:

32
00:01:57,799 --> 00:02:02,878
Scam Gym builds a habit under simulated pressure.

33
00:02:02,878 --> 00:02:06,483
A real caller with a spoofed number may still

34
00:02:06,483 --> 00:02:09,286
sound more convincing than any drill.

35
00:02:09,586 --> 00:02:12,721
Built between October seventeenth and now,

36
00:02:12,721 --> 00:02:16,928
with AI coding assistance from Claude Code.

37
00:02:16,928 --> 00:02:18,861
Scam Gym.

38
00:02:18,861 --> 00:02:22,542
Practice the call before the scammer makes it.
